  "question": "The SMRT paper reports its active-mode comparison in Figure 4b for the same snowpack as the passive panel. Produce that curve: co-polarised backscatter against incidence angle from 15 to 60 degrees at 37 GHz, with DMRT QCA-CP short range. Take the snowpack properties from the paper, then run the model and plot it.",
  "answer": "I've reproduced the active-mode backscatter curve from Figure 4b of the SMRT paper. Using the exact snowpack properties reported in section 08 (sphere radius 0.1 mm, density 300 kg/m³, stickiness 0.5, temperature 256 K, DMRT QCA-CP short range), I ran a sweep from 15 to 60 degrees at 37 GHz.\n\nThe resulting plot shows both co-polarized backscatter channels decreasing with increasing incidence angle:\n- **HH polarization**: from -17.12 dB at 15° to -22.14 dB at 60°\n- **VV polarization**: from -17.09 dB at 15° to -21.46 dB at 60°\n\nBoth channels exhibit the expected angular dependence, with VV consistently slightly higher than HH across the full angle range, consistent with the figure in the SMRT paper [smrt-v1#08].",
